ts stored (sonnet, sol, sol62); cost 7.5384; no debate_errors row after the launch). FIRST RUN, EXERCISED IN PART. The close's line names why: "ROUND: [CR4]; SENT BACK: 0 barred sentence(s); 6 layer point(s); 0 pressed verse(s) with no ANSWER line". No line reads "SENT BACK: 0 sentence(s)". The link round's line names nothing: "ROUND: [CR3]; SENT BACK: 0 barred sentence(s); 0 layer point(s); KEPT: second round (the replacement round (53558 -> 54409 chars; barred sentences 0 -> 0))". W4 reads from code that the round is called again on any of three counts (barred sentences, layer points, pressed verses short of their layers) and that the line prints the third only for the close; the third count is the likely cause, not confirmed (the node's execution was not read). So a second call with no stated reason recurred, in the same class as the defect this ASK answered. NOT CHECKED: that the counts equal the round's own why. W3 does not count this run as one of the two live runs with no issue; objective_met and status are unchanged.$t$,
